<report>
<title>Probit analysis - @title</title>
<p>constant = @{a:roundu}<br />
slope = @{b:roundu}</p>

<p>Median * Dose = @{mxd:roundu}<br />
<ci>Confidence interval @het = @{from:roundu} to @{to:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>* Dose for centile @{centile:roundu} = @{doseq:roundu}<br />
<ci>Confidence interval @het_cent = @{from_cent:roundu} to @{to_cent:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>Chi<sup>2</sup> (heterogeneity of deviations from model) = @{dev:roundu}  (@df df)  <pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>

<p>t for slope = @{t_slope:roundu} (@df df_slope)  <pval>@{p_slope:pval}</pval></p>
<block name="warn">
<p><warn>WARNING: slope not significant</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
